.br
.sp 0.65v
The modelling decisions that matter are these. The scalars are natural numbers s and t, with 2 <= t and t-1 <= s; the threshold is existentially quantified after s and t and before n. Graphs are SimpleGraph (Fin n) with a DecidableRel instance, which covers every graph of order n up to relabelling. Q is adjMatrix R + degMatrix R. qIndex is the supremum of the real spectrum of Q, and qIndex_isGreatest proves it is the greatest element. Freeness is mathlib's Free, i.e., absence of an injective graph homomorphism from the complete bipartite graph, so it is ordinary non-induced containment. printedBound uses real arithmetic throughout, including real subtraction in n-t+1. graphJoin is defined by hand as the disjoint union with all cross edges; K_{t-1} is the complete graph on Fin (t-1); H is a graph on Fin (n-t+1) with IsRegularOfDegree s. The equality clause is placed inside the freeness hypothesis, as in the source sentence and its Theorem 5.
.br
.sp 0.65v
Independent audit. The independent audit rebuilt all nine modules from an empty build and kernel-checked each one; it read every module; it walked the 35,041 constants in the transitive closure of the two main theorems and found no missing constant; the axioms are exactly propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. It proved semantic controls: the triangle has q = 4 and the printed bound at (3,1,2) is 4; the join form of the triangle; K_4 is not C_4-free, and an induced reading would make this false; a free graph (the bowtie) is accepted; four variants of the formula (a sign change, a constant change, the order change n-t for n-t+1, and a truncated subtraction) differ from printedBound; the path on three vertices has q = 3; an explicit no-injective-map form of freeness is equivalent to Free; free_swap; the bowtie's q and bound are (7+sqrt 17)/2; equality for the wheel K_1 join C_4; the scope witnesses of Remark 2.1; and two negative controls, a false claim and a sorry, were rejected with exit 1. The audit trusted upstream Lean and mathlib: it verified hashes of Mathlib.lean and lake-manifest.json against PINS and Lean's version string, not the mathlib revision itself, and not every olean. It compared Conjecture 4 against the text layer of the source, not the page image. The audit was performed by an AI system of the same family as the proof authors, not by a human referee. Its independence was limited: it read the proof and the earlier AI reviews before reaching its view, so this is verification, not independent invention. The audit recorded four defects: a cosmetic docstring reference to a file not in the source-only packet; a low-severity absence of semantic controls beyond qIndex_isGreatest, which the audit supplied; and two informational items, a heartbeat option and the placement of the unconditional reverse direction under freeness. None affects validity or fidelity.
.br
.sp 0.65v
.ne 5v
Status. The audit recommended a technical pass and reported no defect affecting validity or fidelity. The receipts, hashes and mathlib pin of the certificate were verified separately. This is not a human referee report.
.br
