8. Limits
.br
.ft R
.ps 11
.sp 0.5v
.sp 0.65v
The prior-art search behind this paper was bounded, and no citation index was available. Four works were not read: (i) a UFRGS thesis, Indices de grafos livres de K_{s,t}; its title concerns indices of K_{s,t}-free graphs, and if it proves the conjecture then this result is not new; (ii) the final journal version of the source (LAA 496), which was not read; (iii) the body of Yu, Wang and Guo, ELA 30 (2015) 795-811; and (iv) RAIRO Operations Research 10.1051/ro/2023109, which could not be retrieved (HTTP 403) and whose title was never seen.
.br
.sp 0.65v
The nearest printed results read for this paper are the upper bounds of Kong and Wang [2] and the minor-free results of Chen and Zhang [3]; neither gives the exact bound of Theorem 1. These are context, not a novelty clearance. The general witness family in Remark 2.1 is a hand argument checked numerically to n = 40; only the n = 8 case is in Lean. It is a side remark and is not used in the proof of Theorem 1.
.br
.sp 0.65v
Objections to significance. The AI reviews of this work state: the join lemma is a routine adaptation of Proposition 6 of the source; the structural step follows a heavy-vertex template known in adjacency work; the proof is short; and the significance was judged modest. No peer review, priority or worldwide novelty is claimed.
.br
.sp 1v
